acter to make it a  two-parter of sorts so that that you  know again that series wasn't bad but  sort of that using a lot more  two-parters to try and flush stuff out  was maybe a little too much because not  every story actually needs effectively  an hour and a half to tell but there  plenty of stories that could benefit  from just an extra 15 minutes so this is  a move that well it saddens me that I'm  going to get fewer Doctor Who episodes  in a series and that bums me out a  little bit this is an exciting change to  me and it's not guaranteed it's gonna  work getting any change that is made  could go for the better it could go for  the worse but I can see where this is  the potential to give us something a  little bit different that should not  really inherently impact the nature of  Doctor Who and how the stories function  but it could just give them a chance to  be a little richer a little deeper and  that's exciting to me I know I said I  was gonna come back to the interior  TARDIS sonic screwdriver  those aren't huge surprises both of  those got a drastic redesign when we had  the last showrunner changeover when  Steven Moffat came in we had a new  doctor new Cobain completely redesigned  interior TARDIS brand new sonic  screwdriver so bringing Chris Chibnall  in and it's not a huge surprise that  he's gonna do all these other things the  one part of me that's going a little bit  is just because and this is not a reason  not to change these things I think it  would be weirder to actually keep the  old stuff but I I can't help up on the  fact that peep that these changes to the  interior of the TARDIS to the sonic  screwdriver are gonna get scrutinized  way more than would normally happen  because of the already significant  changes that have already been made to  the show of course the big one being  Jodie Whittaker is the doctor now and  and I'm not even just talking about  people who are like not my doctor will  not watch I mean they weren't gonna tune  in